8	/**
9	 * Large tool output → file, for every tool in the session (ours, other extensions', SDK
10	 * customTools, Task results). Mirrors Claude Code's tool-result persistence:
11	 *
12	 * - A result is persisted when its text exceeds the tool's threshold: Claude Code uses
13	 *   min(tool.maxResultSizeChars, 50000) — Grep 20000, Bash 30000, everything else 50000;
14	 *   Read is never persisted. `outputSpill.maxChars` overrides the threshold for every tool.
15	 * - Results containing images are never persisted.
16	 * - The inline replacement is `<persisted-output>` + size + path + a 2KB preview cut at a line break.
17	 * - A successful result with no text at all becomes "(<Tool> completed with no output)".
18	 *
19	 * Implemented as a `tool_result` handler. pi chains `tool_result` handlers in extension load order
20	 * (and registration order within an extension); each handler sees the previous handler's patch.
21	 * This handler therefore sees everything earlier handlers did, but extensions loaded AFTER ours
22	 * run after it.
23	 */
