58	export const TASK_CREATE_DESCRIPTION = `Use this tool to create a structured task list for your current coding session. This helps you track progress, organize complex tasks, and demonstrate thoroughness to the user.
59	It also helps the user understand the progress of the task and overall progress of their requests.
60	
61	## When to Use This Tool
62	
63	Use this tool proactively in these scenarios:
64	
65	- Complex multi-step tasks - When a task requires 3 or more distinct steps or actions
66	- Non-trivial and complex tasks - Tasks that require careful planning or multiple operations
67	- Plan mode - When using plan mode, create a task list to track the work
68	- User explicitly requests todo list - When the user directly asks you to use the todo list
69	- User provides multiple tasks - When users provide a list of things to be done (numbered or comma-separated)
70	- After receiving new instructions - Immediately capture user requirements as tasks
71	- When you start working on a task - Mark it as in_progress BEFORE beginning work
72	- After completing a task - Mark it as completed and add any new follow-up tasks discovered during implementation
73	
74	## When NOT to Use This Tool
75	
76	Skip using this tool when:
77	- There is only a single, straightforward task
78	- The task is trivial and tracking it provides no organizational benefit
79	- The task can be completed in less than 3 trivial steps
80	- The task is purely conversational or informational
81	
82	NOTE that you should not use this tool if there is only one trivial task to do. In this case you are better off just doing the task directly.
83	
84	## Task Fields
85	
86	- **subject**: A brief, actionable title in imperative form (e.g., "Fix authentication bug in login flow")
87	- **description**: What needs to be done
88	- **activeForm** (optional): Present continuous form shown in the spinner when the task is in_progress (e.g., "Fixing authentication bug"). If omitted, the spinner shows the subject instead.
89	
90	All tasks are created with status \`pending\`.
91	
92	## Tips
93	
94	- Create tasks with clear, specific subjects that describe the outcome
95	- After creating tasks, use TaskUpdate to set up dependencies (blocks/blockedBy) if needed
96	- Check TaskList first to avoid creating duplicate tasks
97	`;
