173	- **status**: The task status (see Status Workflow below)
174	- **subject**: Change the task title (imperative form, e.g., "Run tests")
175	- **description**: Change the task description
176	- **activeForm**: Present continuous form shown in spinner when in_progress (e.g., "Running tests")
177	- **owner**: Change the task owner (agent name)
178	- **metadata**: Merge metadata keys into the task (set a key to null to delete it)
179	- **addBlocks**: Mark tasks that cannot start until this one completes
180	- **addBlockedBy**: Mark tasks that must complete before this one can start
181	
182	## Status Workflow
183	
184	Status progresses: \`pending\` → \`in_progress\` → \`completed\`
185	
186	Use \`deleted\` to permanently remove a task.
187	
188	## Staleness
189	
190	Make sure to read a task's latest state using \`TaskGet\` before updating it.
191	
192	## Examples
193	
194	Mark task as in progress when starting work:
195	\`\`\`json
196	{"taskId": "1", "status": "in_progress"}
197	\`\`\`
198	
199	Mark task as completed after finishing work:
200	\`\`\`json
201	{"taskId": "1", "status": "completed"}
202	\`\`\`
203	
204	Delete a task:
205	\`\`\`json
206	{"taskId": "1", "status": "deleted"}
207	\`\`\`
208	
209	Claim a task by setting owner:
210	\`\`\`json
211	{"taskId": "1", "owner": "my-name"}
212	\`\`\`
213	
214	Set up task dependencies:
215	\`\`\`json
216	{"taskId": "2", "addBlockedBy": ["1"]}
217	\`\`\`
218	`;
219	
